  "conclusion": "Largest test-set object occupies 9.3% of its frame; largest training-set object occupies only 1.7% -- a 5.5x gap. The 'recall 0.000 on large targets' finding is dominated by objects genuinely out of the size distribution the model was trained on (chiefly frames 0365_2018 and 0366_2018, area_frac ~9.3%), not primarily a fixable augmentation-tuning artifact. Scale augmentation (E04's factor range ~0.75-1.25x) cannot synthesize a 5x+ linear-dimension jump from typical training crops. This corrects an earlier (Phase 2) hypothesis that attributed the gap mainly to scale-augmentation bias."
